 ## Spec Change Log
 
+- 2026-10-08: Verified the original repair SHA, successful exact-source CI/Commitlint, stable v3.102.0 tag, and all 14 packages in both channels. Release run 33948044490 logs have expired (GitHub HTTP 410), so its bypass input cannot be reconstructed. The user selected fixing current main and publishing a new release. Continue under [the current-main spec](spec-current-ci-release-2026-10-08.md), preserving this historical baseline, frozen intent, and all predecessor bytes. Later aggregate review findings are recorded individually above; demonstrated current-main failures are addressed in that continuation.
+
 ## Review Triage Log
 
+| Finding | Verdict | Route | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| BH01 | high | defer | prepare-oq8-v5-candidate.py archives the packet-reviewed commit and forces a clean flag, so validate_active_snapshot compares historical inputs to themselves. This is a later v5 change, outside the original v3 timestamp repair; changing its sealed verifier requires a governed successor. |
+| BH02 | high | defer | release.yml runs npm ci before npm audit signatures, while the approved shared workflow used --ignore-scripts. This later release rewrite predates the continuation; it is not changed by the three demonstrated CI repairs. |
+| BH03 | medium | defer | oq8-v5-packet.py load_json uses default json.loads and canonical uses default json.dumps; duplicate keys and non-finite numbers are accepted. This later v5 parser did not exist in the original repair. |
+| BH04 | medium | defer | validate_receipts checks that findings are nonblank strings but performs no protected-content check. Later v5 receipt policy remains a separate successor concern. |
+| BH05 | medium | defer | validate_receipts validates evidenceSha256 format without loading a retained artifact. It therefore proves a claimed hash rather than verification bytes; this later v5 receipt contract is unchanged here. |
+| BH06 | high | defer | ExplicitEvidenceArtifactPathPattern accepts any .ctrf.json and every path under 6-1-p1r-3110/verification without hashing. These broad existing exemptions predate this continuation; new fixes must not extend them. |
+| BH07 | high | defer | DecodeTrackedText trusts two-byte MZ and other short signatures before considering the path. A text file can evade scanning. This existing decoder behavior is not caused by archived-data classification fixes. |
+| BH08 | high | defer | IsUsableLiteral returns false for a credential value containing any runtime C# interpolation without inspecting static segments. The reported synthetic-static-prefix case reaches that branch; this pre-existing detection bypass remains separate. |
+| BH09 | high | defer | ContainsUnsafeRuntimeLiteralOperand checks quoted arguments against RuntimeCredentialMaterialPattern, while runtime calls containing an identifier can be recognized as sources. Short literal credential arguments can therefore evade scanning; this pre-existing expression-policy defect is separate. |
+| BH10 | high | defer | IsPythonRuntimeExpression accepts os.environ prefixes and the fallback regex does not inspect Python or branches. A literal fallback can pass. This pre-existing expression-policy defect is separate. |
+| BH11 | high | defer | ContainsUnsafeRuntimeLiteralOperand checks shell parameter defaults, while IsShellRuntimeExpression accepts curl substitutions by prefix. A literal echo fallback can pass. This pre-existing expression-policy defect is separate. |
+| BH12 | high | defer | The JavaScript transform branch checks fallback patterns then returns without inspecting replaceAll replacement literals. A replacement secret can pass. This pre-existing expression-policy defect is separate. |
+| EC01 | medium | continuation | The downloaded Contracts TRX from run 37740386611 records five errors from the exact newly archived Directory.Packages.props omitted from the exemption list. The user authorized fixing current main; the continuation addresses it without changing frozen evidence. |
+| EC02 | medium | continuation | The downloaded Server TRX records package names Microsoft.IdentityModel.JsonWebTokens and Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens as findings. IsPackageDependencyMetadata handles npm files only; the continuation adds structural NuGet controls. |
+| EC03 | high | defer | Independently verified the same release npm lifecycle ordering as BH02. It is grouped with BH02 as one later, pre-existing release-hardening defect. |
+| EC04 | medium | defer | ci.yml already excludes two tests explicitly tagged HeavyweightContainerPublish, and ContainerPublishingGovernanceTests asserts that existing filter. The continuation adds no exclusions and runs full local Contracts; restoring remote heavyweight coverage is a separate existing CI design gap. |
+| VG01 | high | defer | Pre-verified gap: EventStore publication-freeze behavior has no executable regression test, and an in-memory inverted comparison enabled publication for unset/false/True. Later copied release gate remains unchanged here; record a separate regression test task. |
+| VG02 | medium | continuation | Duplicate independently verified archived package-authority failure; grouped with EC01 and addressed by the current-main continuation. |
+| VG03 | medium | continuation | Duplicate independently verified NuGet scanner metadata false positives; grouped with EC02 and addressed by the current-main continuation. |
